    schema:about "Mouse embryonic metanephric kidney ureteric bud & cap mesenchyme (Mus musculus, E11.5-E15.5)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A deforming tetrahedral/FEM mesh of capsule and nephrogenic zone, anisotropic tissue growth, an ellipsoidal kidney, epithelial mechanics, cell-level nephron induction, or quantitative reproduction of the specimen micrograph's pErk1/2 fold (the 2.40 reference is unsourced)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 4-species GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 reaction-diffusion solver on a 1D periodic ampulla ring with m = 1..4 mode selection (L212-L361); a 3D stochastic ureteric tree across g = 1..8 with Horton-Strahler ordering (L366-L457, L655-L914); a steady diffuse-domain GDNF field inside an expanding spherical renal capsule with nephrogenic-zone production shell and RET tip sinks (L526-L604) coupled to the tree by chemotaxis, confinement, interstitial dilation and GDNF-gated arrest; a 6-condition capsule coupling sweep (L990-L1051); a 5-condition perturbation suite at g = 5 (L1057-L1101); colour-threshold segmentation of a vendored E12.5 micrograph (L1107-L1215)",
        "reported_in_source: Menshykau & Iber (2013): a ligand-receptor (GDNF-RET) Schnakenberg-type Turing mechanism on the ureteric bud epithelium selects elongation, bifurcation or trifurcation according to the ampulla geometry; GDNF is produced by the cap mesenchyme and bound by epithelial RET",
        "reported_in_source: Short et al. (2014): OPT tip counts across E11.5-E15.5 (2 to 354 tips), Horton-Strahler R_b 2.08 and R_L 1.38, stereotyped early branching followed by a spatially regulated nephrogenic-zone programme in which all tips reside beneath the renal capsule",
        "reported_in_source: Watanabe & Costantini (2004), Basson et al. (2005), Miyazaki et al. (2000), Shakya et al. (2005): GDNF-bead attraction, Spry1-/- supernumerary budding, BMP4 stalk inhibition and Gdnf-/-/Ret-/- renal agenesis",
        "transfer_boundary: Per-generation segment lengths and branch angles are read from the reference table (L743-L747); the tree reproduces the ordering of tip counts, not an independent prediction of the generation-wise geometry",
        "transfer_boundary: The capsule constants (300/550 um anchors, 110 um nephrogenic zone, 150 um GDNF decay length, kappa_tip 2.0, gate 0.15, chi 0.35) are modelling assumptions tagged as such in renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json, not literature table values",
        "transfer_boundary: The capsule is a sphere on a fixed Eulerian grid with isotropic dilation, not a moving-mesh finite-element model of the kidney; its radius R_cap(g) is prescribed from the Short (2014) observed tip numbers (L509-L519, L750), so the moving boundary is partly data-driven rather than emergent" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Bifurcating vascular / bronchial / hyphal branch in Mus musculus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "6. Tip-Splitting & Flow Trees" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Bifurcating Vascular/Lung Trees" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Murray Law r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.11.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.12.004>,
