<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Code-to-model traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header (L1-L16) states the Pass 3 remediation, names the reduced model and the residual FEM item, and maps each law to its Lean theorem; Section 3b has a banner and the four couplings are numbered (i)-(iv) in comments at the lines where they act; the new JSON's status tags and the `measure_morphoeval` docstring (9 + 3) make the provenance of each number legible. Deductions: the trifurcation / branch-probability constants 0.08 / 0.24 / 0.22, the 1.28 / 0.72 stage factors and 0.99 * gain^0.42 (L705-L709, L772-L778) have no cited source (-4); the `self_test` docstring still reads \"8-check ... Pass 2 (v2)\" although the suite has 9 checks and prints \"Pass 3 v3\" (-2); the GIF's use of dilated positions is not documented (-1); the ampulla ring geometry is called a dome (-1). Net: 92 -> 90." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1825–L1826: Stale `self_test` docstring: '8-check ... Pass 2 (v2)' vs 9 checks / Pass 3 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1825-L1826>",
        "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L705–L709: Untraced trifurcation constants 0.08 / 0.24 / 0.22 and BMP4 0.04 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L705-L709>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The 4-species Schnakenberg GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 PDE (L212-L328), m = 1..4 ampulla mode selection (L331-L361), 3D tree with exact Strahler ordering (L366-L457, L655-L914) and the agenesis / Spry1 controls are unchanged and sound. Pass 3 adds a physically reasonable diffuse-domain GDNF field: production confined to the nephrogenic shell phi_nz, decay and RET tip sinks inside phi_cap, zero GDNF outside the capsule (verified by self-test 9), and four couplings — chemotaxis, confinement, interstitial dilation with the hilum fixed, and GDNF-gated arrest — each of which produces the qualitatively expected effect in the sweep (+3 net vs v2 for the mechanism, backed by 2 new Lean theorems). Deductions, all exposed by the remediation: the capsule radius is prescribed from the Short (2014) observed tip number it is later compared against, so the moving boundary is not an emergent part of the model (-3); R_cap anchors, nephrogenic-zone thickness, GDNF decay length, kappa_tip, the 0.15 gate and chi = 0.35 are order-of-magnitude assumptions, not Menshykau/Short values (-2); the capsule is a sphere with isotropic dilation whereas the kidney is ellipsoidal with anisotropic growth (-1); per-generation segment lengths and angles come from the reference table rather than from the PDE or capsule (-1); the ampulla PDE is a periodic 1D ring of length pi R_tip described as a dome, with m = 1..4 seeded explicitly in the initial bias (-1). Net: 94 -> 90." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L479–L489: CAPSULE_PARAMS: 300/550 um anchors, 110 um NZ, 150 um decay length, kappa_tip 2.0, margin 22 um, hilum offset 0.62 are approximate anchors / modelling assumptions <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L479-L489>",
        "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L509–L519: Capsule radius R_cap(g) interpolated from the OBSERVED Short (2014) tip number of the same generation — the moving boundary is data-prescribed, not emergent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L509-L519>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` returns 12 reference-anchored measurements (9 carried from v2 plus E15.5 tips-in-nephrogenic-zone fraction 0.666 vs ref 1.0 with the decoupled 0.114 stated, capsule-crowding suppression ratio 0.676 vs decoupled null 1.0, and NZ/core GDNF enrichment 2.15 vs uniform null 1.0), each with method, reference source and a note. Short (2014) tip correlation r = 0.9997 (RMSE 23.3 vs 2^g RMSE 38.7), R_b 2.177 (ref 2.08), R_L 1.371 (ref 1.38), Delta m = 1, Spry1/WT and BMP4/WT ratios, agenesis 0 tips, specimen 13/6 tips. Deductions: the E15.5 count is 293 vs 354 observed and the g = 5 WT count 36 vs 40.2 — the Pearson r is dominated by exponential growth and is weak evidence of fit (-3); the segment- length r is circular because the generation lengths are read from the same reference table (-3); R_b passes the 1.90-2.30 self-test window only at gate 0.15 (2.35 at gate 0.18 or chi = 0) and `compute_horton_strahler_metrics` drops the last ratio and falls back to 2.0 (-2); two of the three new measurements are compared with null hypotheses (1.0) rather than measured values (-2); the pErk fold 38.65 vs unsourced 2.40 is reported as a measurement without comment on the 16x gap (-2); spry1 and bead trees differ only via `seed + 10*idx` (-1). Net: 93 -> 86." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1062–L1074: Perturbation suite trees differ only through `seed + 10*idx`; WT g=5 36 vs obs 40.2 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1062-L1074>",
        "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L427–L436: `compute_horton_strahler_metrics` drops the last ratio ('interior') and falls back to R_b = 2.0 when fewer than 2 valid orders <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L427-L436>",
        "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L743–L747: Per-generation `segment_length_um` and `branch_angle_deg` read from the reference table, making the segment-length Pearson r (L956-L957) circular <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L743-L747>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-ampulla-circumferential-harmonic-transition-m-2-bifurcation-m-3-trifurcation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-bmp4-stalk-elongation-inhibition-vs-wild-type-e13-5-tip-suppression-ratio-miyazaki-et-al-2000>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-capsule-crowding-tip-suppression-ratio-n-tips-e15-5-capsule-x0-5-n-tips-e15-5-wt-capsule-pass-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-e15-5-fraction-of-ureteric-tips-inside-the-nephrogenic-zone-phase-field-capsule-coupling-pass-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-gdnf-ret-renal-agenesis-negative-control-tip-count-rho-g-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-horton-strahler-ureteric-segment-length-ratio-r-l-short-et-al-2014-fig-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-horton-strahler-ureteric-tree-bifurcation-ratio-r-b-short-et-al-2014-fig-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-nephrogenic-zone-to-medullary-core-mesenchymal-gdnf-enrichment-ratio-at-e15-5-diffuse-domain-field-pass-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-specimen-e12-5-wild-type-segmented-ureteric-tip-count-kidney-ureteric-tree-specimen-jpg-panel-a>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-specimen-perk1-2-to-cytokeratin-tip-signaling-fold-change-wt-panels-d-f-vs-mutant-panels-g-i>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-spry1-vs-wild-type-e13-5-supernumerary-tip-ratio-basson-et-al-2005-dev-cell>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-measurement-ureteric-tip-count-generational-correlation-across-e11-5-e15-5-short-et-al-2014-g-1-8>,
