<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 88.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py` (overall weighted score 88.1/100, down from 92.8 in v2). The single v2 remediation item — couple the 3D tree to a phase-field / moving-boundary model of the expanding renal capsule and nephrogenic zone — is closed in a reduced, honestly labelled form: a steady diffuse-domain GDNF field on a fixed 36x36x39 grid inside an expanding spherical capsule with a nephrogenic-zone production shell and RET tip sinks, coupled to the tree by chemotaxis, moving-boundary confinement, interstitial dilation and GDNF-gated arrest. The coupling demonstrably matters: 67 % of E15.5 tips lie in the nephrogenic zone (decoupled v2 tree 11 %, with 80 % outside the capsule), a half-rate capsule suppresses the tip count to 198/293 through 103 vs 7 gated arrests, and the field is 2.15x enriched in the nephrogenic zone. Two Lean theorems (confinement bound, crowding-arrest monotonicity) are machine-checked, the self-test grows to 9 checks and 12 measurements, and three CLI flags plus the previously dead --D-ratio are wired. The lower score reflects what the remediation exposed rather than regressions: E15.5 tips 293 vs 354 observed (RMSE 23.3; v2's perfect fit came from a hard-coded WT branch_prob = 1.0 that is now removed), capsule constants that are order-of-magnitude anchors, a capsule radius prescribed from the observed tip counts, self-referential generation lengths/angles, a fragile Horton-Strahler R_b (2.18 at gate 0.15, 2.35 at 0.18), a specimen micrograph from a prorenin-receptor study with an unsourced pErk fold reference, and CLI overrides that do not reach the perturbation suite, sweep or capsule figure. Overall 88.1/100 (faithfulness 87.0, reproducibility 90.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney_comparison.png: rendered output of 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py at 028758bc, image/png, 945447 B, 2742×1446 px, artifact_sha256 9f98460186b4bdf7797ab875a51788dba9d5afea8d89977769eda0675a4efdc0 (sha256 9f98460186b4bdf7797ab875a51788dba9d5afea8d89977769eda0675a4efdc0), spec_fingerprint f9c1a998913eff873333397950c9abd3c6d935d905ec30d2d429a949264e57cf. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: f9c1a998913eff873333397950c9abd3c6d935d905ec30d2d429a949264e57cf; artifact_sha256: 9f98460186b4bdf7797ab875a51788dba9d5afea8d89977769eda0675a4efdc0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney_reference.json=b624d595c12fdf8d..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg=dceaf5044c7014e4..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/paper_citations.bib=3eb2da09bd233938..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json=8959f600edc5b3b8..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/scout_manifest.json=60b78a1876b45c42...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Menshykau & Iber (2013): a ligand-receptor (GDNF-RET) Schnakenberg-type Turing mechanism on the ureteric bud epithelium selects elongation, bifurcation or trifurcation according to the ampulla geometry; GDNF is produced by the cap mesenchyme and bound by epithelial RET | Short et al. (2014): OPT tip counts across E11.5-E15.5 (2 to 354 tips), Horton-Strahler R_b 2.08 and R_L 1.38, stereotyped early branching followed by a spatially regulated nephrogenic-zone programme in which all tips reside beneath the renal capsule | Watanabe & Costantini (2004), Basson et al. (2005), Miyazaki et al. (2000), Shakya et al. (2005): GDNF-bead attraction, Spry1-/- supernumerary budding, BMP4 stalk inhibition and Gdnf-/-/Ret-/- renal agenesis; reconstructed_in_script: 4-species GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 reaction-diffusion solver on a 1D periodic ampulla ring with m = 1..4 mode selection (L212-L361); a 3D stochastic ureteric tree across g = 1..8 with Horton-Strahler ordering (L366-L457, L655-L914); a steady diffuse-domain GDNF field inside an expanding spherical renal capsule with nephrogenic-zone production shell and RET tip sinks (L526-L604) coupled to the tree by chemotaxis, confinement, interstitial dilation and GDNF-gated arrest; a 6-condition capsule coupling sweep (L990-L1051); a 5-condition perturbation suite at g = 5 (L1057-L1101); colour-threshold segmentation of a vendored E12.5 micrograph (L1107-L1215); transfer_boundary: The capsule is a sphere on a fixed Eulerian grid with isotropic dilation, not a moving-mesh finite-element model of the kidney; its radius R_cap(g) is prescribed from the Short (2014) observed tip numbers (L509-L519, L750), so the moving boundary is partly data-driven rather than emergent | Per-generation segment lengths and branch angles are read from the reference table (L743-L747); the tree reproduces the ordering of tip counts, not an independent prediction of the generation-wise geometry | The capsule constants (300/550 um anchors, 110 um nephrogenic zone, 150 um GDNF decay length, kappa_tip 2.0, gate 0.15, chi 0.35) are modelling assumptions tagged as such in renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json, not literature table values; does_not_claim: A deforming tetrahedral/FEM mesh of capsule and nephrogenic zone, anisotropic tissue growth, an ellipsoidal kidney, epithelial mechanics, cell-level nephron induction, or quantitative reproduction of the specimen micrograph's pErk1/2 fold (the 2.40 reference is unsourced)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1193-1198 and 1812-1821 — the pErk1/2 ROIs are hard-coded pixel boxes that ignore `panel_d_f_wt_if_roi_xyxy` in the reference JSON, and the measured fold 38.65 is compared with an unsourced `reference_value: 2.40`. Read the ROIs from the JSON, state a sourced reference or mark the measurement as uncalibrated.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1230-1234, 1589-1597 and 990-997 — CLI overrides reach only the g=1..8 tree; the perturbation suite, Panel H sweep and the capsule figure take `seed` only, and the `no_capsule` ablation changes chemotaxis, confinement, gate and dilation at once. Propagate overrides and add single-factor ablations (confinement-only, gate-only, dilation-only).",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1622-1678 — `render_growth_gif` draws every generation frame with the final (dilated) node positions, so early frames show already-stretched segments. Record per-generation node snapshots during growth and animate those.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1798 and datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/paper_citations.bib — Shakya et al. (2005) Dev. Cell 8:65-74 is cited in a measurement source string but absent from the bib; add it (and update the SHA-256 pin) and verify the DOI 10.1016/j.devcel.2004.11.008.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1807-1808 and datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney_reference.json — the vendored Wikimedia micrograph is from a prorenin-receptor (PRR UB-/-) study, not a GDNF/RET or Short (2014) specimen, and the \"published 12 tips, cohort mean 13.2 +/- 0.5\" has no verifiable citation. Either vendor a CC-licensed GDNF/RET-perturbation specimen or relabel the panel as a generic E12.5 ureteric tree.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1826 — `self_test` docstring says \"8-check ... Pass 2 (v2)\" while the suite has 9 checks and prints \"Pass 3 v3\"; the ampulla PDE geometry at 232-260 is a periodic 1D ring described as a \"semicircular dome\". Update both docstrings.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:427-436 and 1849 — `compute_horton_strahler_metrics` drops the last ratio and falls back to R_b = 2.0, and the 1.90-2.30 self-test window passes only at gate 0.15 (R_b = 2.35 at gate 0.18 or chi = 0). Compute R_b by log-linear regression over all orders with >= 2 streams and report its sensitivity to the gate.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:479-489 and datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json:15-28 — the capsule anchors (300 / 550 um), nephrogenic-zone thickness 110 um, GDNF decay length 150 um, kappa_tip 2.0, gate 0.15, chi 0.35, hilum offset 0.62 and margin 22 um are tagged as assumptions. Trace at least the capsule radii and nephrogenic-zone thickness to a measured source (Short 2014 OPT volumes or a histology table) and add a sensitivity sweep over gate and chi showing how R_b and the tip count respond.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:509-519 and 750 — `renal_capsule_radius_um` interpolates R_cap(g) from the OBSERVED Short (2014) tip number of the same generation, so the moving boundary is data-prescribed and the Panel C tip-count comparison is not independent of the reference. Drive the capsule radius from simulated state (e.g. cumulative tip count or an interstitial growth law R_cap(t) with its own anchor) and report the comparison as a prediction.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:705-709 and 772-778 — trifurcation constants 0.08 / 0.24 / 0.22, stage factors 1.28 / 0.72 and branch probability 0.99 * gain^0.42 have no cited source; the E15.5 tip count is 293 vs 354 observed (RMSE 23.3) and g=5 WT is 36 vs 40.2. Either calibrate these against the Short (2014) table with the calibration stated, or expose them as documented parameters.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:743-747 and 956-957 — per-generation `segment_length_um` and `branch_angle_deg` are read from the reference table, so the segment-length Pearson r is circular; recorded generation lengths are at formation while Strahler lengths include later dilation (752-761). Derive segment length from the ampulla PDE / capsule geometry or drop the length correlation from the measurement list.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:752-761 and 526-604 — the capsule is a sphere on a fixed Eulerian grid with isotropic dilation; the kidney is ellipsoidal with anisotropic growth and the ureteric epithelium is not a separate phase. Residual of the v2 item: implement a deforming (moving-mesh) capsule / nephrogenic-zone domain or at least an ellipsoidal capsule with anisotropic dilation." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.81e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 adds a 6-condition capsule coupling sweep (coupled, no-chemotaxis, decoupled, capsule x0.6 / x0.5 / x1.3) whose outputs move monotonically with capsule growth (198 < 268 < 293 tips; NZ fraction 0.95 > 0.90 > 0.67 > 0.58), the `grow_ureteric_tree_3d` signature exposes `capsule_growth`, `chemotaxis_weight`, `capsule_confinement`, `gdnf_gate` (L663-L666), `evaluate_short_2014_generations` forwards them, and the CLI gains `--capsule-growth`, `--chemotaxis`, `--no-capsule` while `--D-ratio` (dead in v2) is now wired. The 4 ampulla regimes, 8 generations and 5 perturbation conditions are retained. Deductions: CLI overrides affect only the g = 1..8 tree (Panels A, C, F, G); the perturbation suite, Panel H sweep and the capsule figure take `seed` only and ignore them (-4); the `no_capsule` ablation changes chi, confinement, gate and dilation simultaneously, so only `no_chemotaxis` isolates a single coupling (-3); the gate value 0.15 is not sweepable from the CLI although R_b is sensitive to it (-1). Net: 92 -> 90." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1230–L1234: `render_comparison_figure` passes overrides only to the ampulla modes and the g=1..8 tree; `evaluate_perturbation_suite(seed)` and `evaluate_capsule_coupling_sweep(seed)` ignore them <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1230-L1234>",
        "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L993–L993: `no_capsule` condition sets chemotaxis 0, capsule False and gate 0 at once — a conflated ablation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L993-L993>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`--self-test` passes 9 checks in 6.9 s (SHA-256 integrity of 5 files + capsule JSON consistency, Turing criterion, harmonics [1,2,3,4], Short scaling and Strahler windows, agenesis control, perturbation ordering, specimen segmentation, two-run bitwise determinism of PDE, tree and field, and the new 10-assertion capsule-coupling check including the hilum fixed point and zero GDNF outside the capsule); `measure_morphoeval()` length is asserted (12); the full default render writes the PNG, the capsule PNG and the GIF in 7.3 s; all outputs are seeded and deterministic. Deductions: the self_test docstring is stale (-1); the R_b window 1.90-2.30 is satisfied only at the default gate so the determinism guarantee is narrower than it looks (-1); the capsule figure and sweep cannot be regenerated under the CLI overrides (-1); no pinned requirements lock file for this script (-1). Net: 93 -> 93." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Source and data traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/` carries 5 primary DOIs in `paper_citations.bib`, the scout manifest, the reference JSON, the specimen image and now `renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json`, all 5 SHA-256-pinned and verified fail-closed at every run (`verify_dataset_integrity`, L87-L104; `load_capsule_reference` cross-checks the JSON against `CAPSULE_PARAMS`, L107-L119). The new JSON tags every capsule constant with a status string (approximate anchor / modelling assumption / numerical), which is the right way to disclose unsourced values. Deductions: Shakya et al. (2005) is cited in a measurement source string (L1798) but is absent from `paper_citations.bib` (-2); the specimen \"published 12 tips, cohort mean 13.2 +/- 0.5\" (L1808) and the pErk reference 2.40 (L1817-L1818) have no verifiable citation (-3); none of the capsule constants is traced to a table or figure (-2). Net: 95 -> 88." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1798–L1818: Shakya 2005 cited but not in the bib; specimen 'cohort mean 13.2 +/- 0.5' and pErk reference 2.40 unsourced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1798-L1818>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Morphological realism / specimen match: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The 8-panel figure now shows the coupled 3D tree, the ampulla modes, the g = 1..8 scaling, the perturbation suite, the specimen segmentation, a mid-plane capsule GDNF slice with capsule / nephrogenic-zone contours and confined tips (Panel G), and the ablation bars (Panel H); the dedicated capsule-coupling figure contrasts the E13.0 and E15.5 coupled trees with the decoupled v2 tree, 80 % of whose tips lie outside the nominal capsule — a visually convincing demonstration that the coupling is what keeps tips in the nephrogenic zone. Specimen segmentation still finds 13 WT vs 6 mutant tips. Deductions, which the v2 audit did not apply: the vendored Wikimedia micrograph is from a prorenin-receptor (PRR UB-/-) study, not a GDNF/RET or Short (2014) specimen, so the \"mutant\" panel is not the Gdnf/Ret perturbation the model simulates (-4); the measured pErk1/2 fold of 38.65 is compared with a reference of 2.40 whose source string is unsourced, a 16x discrepancy left unexplained (-3); the pErk ROIs are hard-coded pixel boxes that ignore the ROI stored in the reference JSON (-1); the GIF draws every generation frame with the final dilated node positions, so early frames show already-stretched segments (-1); the E15.5 coupled tree has 293 tips vs the 354 the figure's own Panel C reports as observed (-2). Net: 91 -> 84." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1622–L1678: GIF uses final (dilated) node positions for every generation frame <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1622-L1678>",
        "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1812–L1821: pErk1/2 fold 38.65 vs `reference_value: 2.40` whose source is an unsourced description string; specimen is from a PRR study, not GDNF/RET <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1812-L1821>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

