<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) Ureteric Ampulla Dichotomous vs Trichotomous Mode Selection Law" ;
    dct:description "Predicts the transition from canonical dichotomous bifurcation (88% of wild-type E11.5-E15.5 events) to trichotomous ampulla splitting when tip swelling exceeds the m=3 harmonic threshold | Variables: R_tip: ureteric ampulla tip radius; ℓ_c = λ_c / (2π): critical Turing length scale; m*: dominant circumferential splitting harmonic (m=2 bifurcation vs m=3 trifurcation)" ;
    dct:source "Menshykau & Iber (2013) Phys. Biol. 10:046003 Figs. 3-5; Short et al. (2014) Dev. Cell 29:188-202 Figs. 2-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L212-L361>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_055_gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney.lean#L49-L65> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ureteric_tip_harmonic_mode (k2_R_tip ell_c : Nat) : Nat :=
  if ell_c == 0 then 0
  else if k2_R_tip < 2 * ell_c then 1
  else if k2_R_tip < 3 * ell_c then 2
  else 3
theorem menshykau_ureteric_tip_mode_selection (ell_c excess : Nat) :
    ureteric_tip_harmonic_mode 20 10 = 2 ∧
    ureteric_tip_harmonic_mode 32 10 = 3 ∧
    ureteric_tip_harmonic_mode (3 * (ell_c + 1) + excess) (ell_c + 1) = 3
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "m* = argmax_m Re(λ(k_m)),  k_m = m / R_tip:  2 ℓ_c ≤ k_2 R_tip < 3 ℓ_c ⇒ m* = 2 (lateral bifurcation);  k_2 R_tip ≥ 3 ℓ_c ⇒ m* = 3 (planar/tetrahedral trifurcation)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.11.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.12.004>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2014.02.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.09.019>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/10/4/046003>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI8256> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Schnakenberg-Type GDNF-RET Cooperative Ligand-Receptor Turing Reaction-Diffusion & Horton-Strahler Ureteric Tree Branching" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_055.ureteric_tip_harmonic_mode" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_055.menshykau_ureteric_tip_mode_selection" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Watanabe & Costantini (2004) & Basson et al. (2005) Gdnf-/-/Ret-/- Renal Agenesis & Spry1-/- Ectopic Budding Law" ;
    dct:description "Accounts for complete renal agenesis in Gdnf-/- or Ret-/- null kidneys and supernumerary ectopic budding upon Sprouty1 deletion | Variables: ρ_G: mesenchymal GDNF synthesis rate; γ_R: effective RET receptor gain modulated by Sprouty1 antagonism; v_tip: normal tip outgrowth velocity; N_tips: terminal ureteric bud tip count" ;
    dct:source "Watanabe & Costantini (2004) Dev. Biol. 271:98-106; Basson et al. (2005) Dev. Cell 8:229-239" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L655-L1101>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_055_gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney.lean#L78-L90> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ureteric_tip_growth_flux (rho_G gamma_R : Nat) : Nat :=
  if rho_G == 0 then 0 else rho_G + gamma_R
theorem menshykau_gdnf_ret_agenesis_and_spry1_budding (rho_G gamma_wt d_gamma : Nat) :
    ureteric_tip_growth_flux 0 gamma_wt = 0 ∧
    ureteric_tip_growth_flux (rho_G + 1) (gamma_wt + d_gamma + 1) >
      ureteric_tip_growth_flux (rho_G + 1) gamma_wt
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "v_tip ∝ ρ_G γ_R max(0, R²G - C_th):  ρ_G = 0 ⇒ v_tip = 0 (renal agenesis);  γ_R(Spry1-/-) = γ_wt + Δγ > γ_wt ⇒ N_tips(Spry1-/-) > N_tips(WT)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.11.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.12.004>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2014.02.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.09.019>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/10/4/046003>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI8256> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Schnakenberg-Type GDNF-RET Cooperative Ligand-Receptor Turing Reaction-Diffusion & Horton-Strahler Ureteric Tree Branching" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_055.ureteric_tip_growth_flux" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_055.menshykau_gdnf_ret_agenesis_and_spry1_budding" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Pass 3 Reduced Phase-Field Renal Capsule Moving-Boundary Tip Confinement Law" ;
    dct:description "Moving-boundary coupling of the 3D ureteric tree to the expanding phase-field capsule: tips are advected with the interstitial dilation of the mesenchyme and can never leave the capsule, so terminal tips accumulate in the peripheral nephrogenic zone (coupled 0.67 vs decoupled v2 tree 0.11 in zone / 80% outside the capsule) | Variables: R_cap(g): expanding renal capsule radius (surface area linear in Short et al. 2014 observed tip number); c(g): capsule centre distal to the ureteric stalk tip; ε: phase-field interface width; margin: minimal tip-to-capsule distance; r: tip radial coordinate" ;
    dct:source "Short et al. (2014) Dev. Cell 29:188-202 Figs. 1 & 4 (tips confined to the nephrogenic zone); Menshykau & Iber (2013) Phys. Biol. 10:046003 (mesenchymal GDNF domain); diffuse-domain phase-field reduction of the Pass 2 FEM remediation item" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L459-L652>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_055_gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney.lean#L107-L118> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def capsule_confine (r R_cap margin : Nat) : Nat :=
  if r + margin ≤ R_cap then r else R_cap - margin
theorem menshykau_capsule_confinement_bound (r R_cap margin : Nat) (h : margin ≤ R_cap) :
    capsule_confine r R_cap margin + margin ≤ R_cap ∧
    (r + margin ≤ R_cap → capsule_confine r R_cap margin = r)
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "phi_cap(x,g) = ½(1 + tanh((R_cap(g) − |x − c(g)|)/ε));  4π R_cap(g)² = A_0 + s·(N_obs(g) − 2);  tip radial position r ↦ r if r + margin ≤ R_cap else R_cap − margin  ⇒  r_tip + margin ≤ R_cap for all tips" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.11.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.12.004>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2014.02.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.09.019>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/10/4/046003>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI8256> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Schnakenberg-Type GDNF-RET Cooperative Ligand-Receptor Turing Reaction-Diffusion & Horton-Strahler Ureteric Tree Branching" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_055.capsule_confine" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_055.menshykau_capsule_confinement_bound" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Pass 3 Nephrogenic-Zone GDNF-Gated Branching Crowding-Arrest Law" ;
    dct:description "Couples tip number to capsule expansion: a slowly expanding capsule crowds the nephrogenic zone, depletes GDNF at the tips and arrests branching (E15.5 tips 198 at ×0.5 capsule vs 293 at WT capsule), while un-gated tips reproduce the Pass 2 geometric tree | Variables: G: diffuse-domain mesenchymal GDNF; φ_nz: nephrogenic-zone (cap mesenchyme) production shell; T(x): smoothed indicator of RET-expressing tips; κ_tip: ligand uptake per tip; n: local crowding number; G_th: branching gate (fraction of tip-free NZ level)" ;
    dct:source "Menshykau & Iber (2013) Phys. Biol. 10:046003 (ligand depletion by receptor binding); Short et al. (2014) Dev. Cell 29:188-202 (nephrogenic-zone tip packing); Pass 3 diffuse-domain reduction" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L526-L604>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_055_gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney.lean#L130-L151> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def nz_tip_branches (rho kappa n G_th : Nat) : Bool :=
  decide (G_th * (1 + kappa * n) ≤ rho)
theorem menshykau_capsule_crowding_arrest_monotone (rho kappa n G_th : Nat) :
    (nz_tip_branches rho kappa (n + 1) G_th = true → nz_tip_branches rho kappa n G_th = true) ∧
    nz_tip_branches rho kappa n 0 = true ∧
    (rho < G_th * (1 + kappa * n) → nz_tip_branches rho kappa n G_th = false)
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "0 = D ∇·(φ_cap ∇G) + ρ_G φ_nz − δ φ_cap G − κ_tip T(x) G;  G_tip ≈ ρ/(1 + κ n);  tip branches iff G_th (1 + κ n) ≤ ρ  (monotone: branching with n+1 neighbours ⇒ branching with n)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.11.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.12.004>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2014.02.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.09.019>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/10/4/046003>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI8256> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Schnakenberg-Type GDNF-RET Cooperative Ligand-Receptor Turing Reaction-Diffusion & Horton-Strahler Ureteric Tree Branching" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_055.nz_tip_branches" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_055.menshykau_capsule_crowding_arrest_monotone" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

